---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"

const marks = [
  { x: 344, time: "1:00", top: true },
  { x: 185, time: "12:30", top: false },
  { x: 105.5, time: "12:15", top: true },
  { x: 65.75, time: "12:07:30", top: false },
]
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="grim-reaper"
  lead="There are reapers after noon, but no earliest one."
>
  <SvgFigure
    name="grim-reaper-timeline"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg"
    viewBox="0 0 390 166"
    title="An endless series of reaper times accumulating immediately after noon"
    desc="Time moves right from noon to 1pm. Reapers act at 1pm, 12:30pm, 12:15pm, 12:07:30pm and repeatedly halfway closer to noon. Many earlier times are marked near noon; every reaper time has another reaper time even closer to noon. There is no first reaper after noon."
  >
    <g fill="none" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="2">
      <path d="M26 96 H366 m-7 -5 7 5 -7 5" />
      <path d="M26 86 V106" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="15">
      <text x="26" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Noon</text>
      <text x="344" y="127" text-anchor="middle">1pm</text>
      <text x="196" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">Later →</text>
    </g>
    <!-- 12:03:45 is still a separate dot. From 12:01:52.5 onward,
         the gaps fall below the six-pixel dot diameter. Show these
         ever-closer marks as a short band reaching their limit at noon. -->
    <circle cx="45.875" cy="96" r="3" fill={series.red} />
    <path d="M26 96 H35.9375" fill="none" stroke={series.red} stroke-width="6" />
    {marks.map(({ x, time, top }) => (
      <g>
        <path d={"M" + x + " 82 V111"} stroke={series.red} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <circle cx={x} cy="96" r="5" fill={series.red} />
        <text
          x={x}
          y={top ? 72 : 147}
          text-anchor="middle"
          fill="currentColor"
          font-size="14"
        >
          {time}
        </text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="42" y="49" fill="currentColor" font-size="15">…</text>
  </SvgFigure>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    If the man lives past noon, some reaper should kill him. Yet no reaper can be the
    first to do so: another is always scheduled earlier. The arrangement is inconsistent.
    Whether that rules out endless causal chains generally remains disputed.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
